YARG OS
=======

An unofficial community project. It is not made, endorsed or supported by the YARG / YARC team. YARG itself is not
part of this system: it is downloaded on the device from YARC's own releases.

The scripts and programs written for this project are under the MIT licence. The system is built with Buildroot and
contains many other programs and libraries under their own licences: the Linux kernel (GPL-2.0), systemd, glibc and
many libraries (LGPL-2.1+), busybox, util-linux and other tools (GPL), Mesa (MIT), and binary firmware and processor
microcode (linux-firmware, intel-microcode; redistributable under the licence texts that come with them).

Each system release is published together with a "legal" file holding the licence texts of everything in it and the
source code of the GPL / LGPL parts (and a link to the exact source tree of the project itself):

    https://github.com/siesta5787/yargos/releases

Names such as PlayStation, Wii, Xbox, Guitar Hero and Rock Band belong to their owners. This system makes some
instruments look like standard PlayStation instruments to YARG, because that is what YARG understands.
